<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Everything else in this app's Info.plist is generated from the
	  INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings. App Transport Security is here because it
	  is a nested dictionary and has no INFOPLIST_KEY_ equivalent; Xcode merges
	  the generated keys into this file.

	  NSAllowsLocalNetworking permits cleartext HTTP to local destinations only:
	  link-local addresses, .local names, and the private ranges. It changes
	  nothing about connections to the internet, which stay under the full ATS
	  rules, and it is the key Apple documents for exactly this case.

	  It exists because development happens against a server on the LAN. That
	  server is fronted by Caddy over TLS from a private CA, and reaching it that
	  way means installing that CA on every device AND enabling it under
	  Settings › General › About › Certificate Trust Settings — a second step
	  that is easy to miss and whose failure looks like "the certificate is
	  invalid" rather than like a missing switch. feed-engine also listens on
	  8081 without TLS, so a development build can point straight at it and skip
	  the certificate entirely. Nothing ships pointing there: the base URL is
	  https://f33d3r.com in release, and only DEBUG reads F33D3R_BASE_URL.

	  The trade is that on a development LAN the session token travels in the
	  clear. That is a development network, and the alternative is a device that
	  cannot be developed against at all.
	-->
	<!--
	  Background audio. `INFOPLIST_KEY_UIBackgroundModes = audio` is set in the
	  build settings and produces no key in the built Info.plist, so the mode was
	  never actually declared: MusicPlayer asks for `.longFormAudio` and puts a
	  track on the lock screen, and iOS then stopped it the moment the app left
	  the foreground. Declared here, where it takes effect.
	-->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
	</array>
	<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
